  "bind_marker": "Sizing",
  "quirks": {
    "lineage": "Modular-architecture AVP build; menu skeleton identical to hummod_3.0.4 (Stop=6, Go 12-30, Trauma/Hemorrhage=741); verified by engine_smoke with the 3.0.4 profile. Ships Model Solver.exe + ScriptedController.exe.",
    "app_title": "HumMod : Integrative Biomedicine (v3.1.0) - the AVP engine is actually HumMod v3.1.0 (window title, verified 2026-11 R1 baseline run).",
    "auto_profile_unreachable": "_detect_profile matches its Trauma/Sizing menu to hummod_3.0.4, so this profile is only used when a server is started with HUMMOD_PROFILE=avphummod. Functionally harmless: menu ids and quirks are identical to 3.0.4 (R1 full-parameter run passed with the 3.0.4 profile).",
    "page_labels_owner_drawn": true,
    "variable_names_differ_from_304": "SOL group names differ from 3.0.4: PO2Veins/CO2Veins (not *Vens), O2Artys/O2Veins.[O2], A2Pool.[A2(pMol/L)], FAPool, KAPool, TriglyceridePool, BodyH2O.TotalVol(L) (TBW), PeripheralResistance.TPR, CollectingDuct_H2O.Outflow (urine flow), organ consumption in *-Fuel.TotalGlucoseUsed(mG/Min)/FAUsed(mG/Min)/KAUsed(mG/Min). See out/experiments/baseline_avp/基线参数表.md.",
    "epo_computed": true,
    "no_clinic_menu": "Top-level menus: Circulation, Respiration, Metabolism, Body Fluids, Electrolytes, Hormones, ... Gender, Nervous System, Acid-Base, Heat, Miscellaneous, Organs, Lifestyle, Diagnosis, Intervention, Trauma, Pathology, Context, Sizing. Manual's Clinic->Chart is the startup Chart page (via '<' '>' pager).",
    "slider_commits": true,
    "slider_pages": "MEASURED 2026-11-05 (R3, avphummod v3.1.0): the Lifestyle/Diet/Goal steppers DO commit - R2's 'do NOT commit at any position' note was wrong (it was the MCP client that could not pass the integer pos). Bridge.set_slider's sequence (SB_THUMBPOSITION to the parent + SB_ENDSCROLL x2) commits the model value, and so do SB_LINERIGHT bursts and WM_LBUTTONDOWN/UP on the arrow buttons. The page has 9 scrollbars: 10013 Carbo's, 10016 Fat, 10019 Protein (kCal) and 10033 Salt, 10036 KCl, 10039 Dietary K++, 10042 Ca++, 10045 PO4--, 10048 SO4-- (mMol/Day). The electrolyte steppers share one irregular index->value scale: 0..10 -> 0..10, 11..39 -> 20..300 (+10/index), 40..43 -> 350/400/450/500, 44..47 -> 750/1000/1250/1500 (1500 = max). Ca++ is 1:1 (index == value). Use hummod_set_param(value=...) or hummod_slider(value=...) - the profile carries the measured table (slider_value_lists). Hormones/Renin/A2: 6781 Level, 6792 Block(%) (index == percent, clamped at 100), 6804 Pump Setting.",
    "radio_pages": "R2 field trial: Lifestyle/Posture ordinal 7 of 8 = Request Standing (PostureControl.Request=3, Status.Posture=3); Lifestyle/Exercise/Control ordinal 2 of 3 = Treadmill (Status.Treadmill=1); Lifestyle/Exercise/Treadmill ordinal 0 of 2 = Walk (Exercise-Treadmill.RunOrWalk=0); Lifestyle/Diet/Control ordinal 3 of 4 = H2O Fixed Intake (DietIntakeH2O.Fixed?=1; H2O radios 10136/10138 DO expose check state). All other radios keep state in the model only - verify with probe_vars.",
    "model_noise": true,
    "avp_diet_goal_semantics": "AVP v3.1.0 has ONE salt goal, not QCP's three sliders: DietGoalElectrolytes.Salt_mMol/Day drives Na+_mMol/Day, and Cl-_mMol/Day = Salt + KCl. So the manual's (Na, Cl) pairs map to (Salt, KCl) = (20, 20) low, (180, 20) normal, (500, 0) high (KCl must go to 0 for Cl=500, which also drops K+ intake 70 -> 50).",
    "a2_floor": "A2Pool formula is 'A2CONC * FormationRate MAX 0.8' (3.0.4 uses MAX 2.5), so full ACE inhibition floors plasma AII at 0.8 pg/mL (0.765 pMol/L), not 0 as measured on QCP 2005.",
    "a2page_controls": "Hormones/Renin/A2 (menu id 222): Pool groupbox with Clamp Off/On radios 6777/6779, Level stepper 6781, Block(%) stepper 6792; Pump groupbox with Switch Off/On radios 6800/6802 and Setting stepper 6804. Block(%) drives CEActivity = CEBase*(1-Block/100), so 100 -> CEActivity 0 -> AII generation 0.",
    "salt_solve_time": "A 1-week Go step takes ~22-27 s for the normal/high-salt arms but 1.5-4 min for the low-salt arms (tighter volume/ADH feedback -> smaller integration steps). The low-salt runs exceed the MCP client's 30 s request timeout: issue the Go, then poll hummod_busy until the status bar says 'Solving ... Done'."
  },
